WEBVTT

00:01.202 --> 00:04.437
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.633 --> 00:07.902
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.936 --> 00:11.639
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.673 --> 00:14.809
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.843 --> 00:17.978
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.013 --> 00:21.148
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.183 --> 00:22.883
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.918 --> 00:24.685
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.720 --> 00:26.189
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.197 --> 00:36.363
Morning, Stella.

00:36.398 --> 00:37.431
Morning, Peter.

00:37.466 --> 00:39.200
Hey, listen, I-I got to
ask you something.

00:39.234 --> 00:41.035
Last night, I heard,
uh, the song

00:41.069 --> 00:42.703
"Pour Some Sugar On Me,"

00:42.738 --> 00:44.905
and-and this question
popped into my head.

00:44.940 --> 00:47.508
Are you-- and please say
yes-- are you related--

00:47.542 --> 00:50.044
and even if you're not, please
say yes-- are you related to--

00:50.078 --> 00:52.012
and please say yes
because I need the attention

00:52.047 --> 00:54.915
from my friends-- are you
related to Def Leppard?

00:54.950 --> 00:56.484
Griffin, can I talk
to you privately?

00:56.518 --> 00:58.352
Stella, turn around.

00:58.386 --> 01:01.288
You know, that is one nice thing
about having a deaf coworker.

01:01.323 --> 01:03.858
Well, that and I can work
on my verbal sound effects

01:03.892 --> 01:05.126
and not feel
self-conscious about

01:05.160 --> 01:06.694
the ones that aren't
quite there yet.

01:06.728 --> 01:08.429
What are you talking about?

01:08.463 --> 01:11.165
I'm talking about this:
shabba dabba dabba dabba dabba.

01:11.199 --> 01:12.900
That's a helicopter
hovering over a woman

01:12.934 --> 01:14.135
swimming in her pool.

01:14.169 --> 01:15.269
I also do animals.

01:15.303 --> 01:16.470
Here's a mouse.

01:16.505 --> 01:18.372
(high-pitched):
Mouse?

01:18.406 --> 01:19.974
Oh, that one's ready.

01:20.008 --> 01:21.809
Griffin, I actually
came to tell you

01:21.843 --> 01:24.311
that you're being promoted
to forklift operator.

01:24.346 --> 01:25.746
Really? That's awesome!

01:25.781 --> 01:27.715
Yeah, Frank retired, and
since you're already required

01:27.749 --> 01:28.949
to wear a helmet here--

01:28.984 --> 01:30.651
which, by the way,
put on your helmet.

01:30.685 --> 01:31.819
Oh, sorry.

01:31.853 --> 01:33.487
Anyway, the job is yours.

01:33.522 --> 01:35.656
Which means you'll be
receiving a five percent raise.

01:35.690 --> 01:37.191
Wow, a raise!

01:37.225 --> 01:39.727
I guess this means I can
afford to set up this cutaway

01:39.761 --> 01:41.829
with a fancy
new transition.

01:41.863 --> 01:43.864
<i>SINGERS:
♪ Cutaway ♪</i>

01:45.634 --> 01:47.134
(motor starts)

01:52.674 --> 01:53.908
<i>SINGERS:
♪ End of cutaway ♪</i>

01:55.877 --> 01:59.413
All right, you beautiful
bastard, show me what you got.

01:59.447 --> 02:01.448
(engine starts)

02:08.990 --> 02:10.191
Peter, you can run now,

02:10.225 --> 02:12.026
and no one will
call you a quitter.

02:12.060 --> 02:13.460
What am I saying? No.

02:13.495 --> 02:16.530
I learned how to use stickers,
and I can learn how to use this.

02:31.213 --> 02:32.713
(forklift beeping)

02:35.584 --> 02:37.318
(forklift beeping)

02:37.352 --> 02:38.853
Oh, this is awesome.

02:38.887 --> 02:40.888
♪

02:57.706 --> 02:59.039
Oh, guys, good,
you're here.

02:59.074 --> 03:01.508
I am so excited.
Guess what.

03:01.543 --> 03:03.277
I hope this isn't
about your podcast again.

03:03.311 --> 03:04.745
Why? Did you
finally listen to it?

03:04.779 --> 03:06.614
Yeah, it was just
15 minutes of you listing

03:06.648 --> 03:08.415
all the hats
you could think of.

03:08.450 --> 03:10.251
Sherlock Holmes hat.

03:10.285 --> 03:11.719
Football man hat.

03:11.753 --> 03:14.321
Angry working-class
Irish idiot hat.

03:14.356 --> 03:17.625
Underwear 'cause you're a cat
in the laundry basket hat.

03:17.659 --> 03:20.327
Vietnamese the sun
is my enemy hat.

03:20.362 --> 03:24.164
Halloween mask that
I flip up to eat my candy hat.

03:24.199 --> 03:27.001
College guy wearing
a pizza box hat.

03:27.035 --> 03:28.569
Blue hat.

03:28.603 --> 03:30.671
I think that's all the hats.

03:30.705 --> 03:32.106
No, you guys, this
is really big.

03:32.140 --> 03:33.207
You're not gonna
believe this.

03:33.241 --> 03:34.341
Peter, we've
been over this.

03:34.376 --> 03:35.609
You're not
allowed to say that

03:35.644 --> 03:37.111
unless there's
a forklift outside.

03:38.880 --> 03:40.080
BOTH:
Forklift!

03:41.116 --> 03:42.283
Wow!

03:42.317 --> 03:43.484
I know,
awesome, right?

03:43.518 --> 03:45.185
Oh, my God,
I want to get on!

03:45.220 --> 03:47.855
Hold on, remember the first
thing we said we'd do.

03:50.392 --> 03:51.592
Wow.

03:51.626 --> 03:53.627
So that's what the
tops of cars look like.

03:53.662 --> 03:55.162
All right,
walking speed.

03:57.432 --> 03:58.465
Afternoon, ma'am.

03:58.500 --> 04:00.100
Afternoon to you,
normal sir.

04:00.135 --> 04:01.769
(whispers):
No one can tell.

04:03.138 --> 04:05.806
Uh, how's the weather
down there, you short idiot?

04:05.840 --> 04:07.541
Should we tell him
his pants fell off?

04:07.575 --> 04:08.976
No, let's wait awhile.

04:09.010 --> 04:11.679
♪ Well you can tell by
the way I use my walk ♪

04:11.713 --> 04:14.882
♪ I walk all the time,
'cause my legs can walk. ♪

04:14.916 --> 04:16.917
♪

04:29.998 --> 04:32.533
Uh, are you gonna
stay for the bris?

04:32.567 --> 04:34.401
Nah, I don't
want to see that.

04:36.438 --> 04:38.839
This whale's
beached himself.

04:38.873 --> 04:41.342
He needs to get back
in the water or he'll die.

04:41.376 --> 04:42.843
PETER: Step aside,
I'll handle this.

04:42.877 --> 04:44.311
Give me some room.

04:44.346 --> 04:47.314
(crowd cheering)

04:56.958 --> 04:58.158
(crowd gasps)

04:58.193 --> 05:00.160
(forklift whirring)

05:47.108 --> 05:48.442
(forklift beeps)

05:52.480 --> 05:55.449
(forklift beeping)

05:55.483 --> 05:58.185
You're whale-come.
(giggles)

05:58.219 --> 05:59.553
Aw, cool shell.

06:13.535 --> 06:16.003
Ah, this is what it's
all about, huh, Duke?

06:16.037 --> 06:19.073
600 gallons of beer
in one big thing.

06:19.107 --> 06:21.008
This is what
we do, Peter.

06:21.042 --> 06:22.876
You know, I always thought
I could chug that,

06:22.911 --> 06:25.145
but I never tried 'cause
I figured I couldn't lift it.

06:25.180 --> 06:26.613
Until now.

06:26.648 --> 06:28.749
Are you nuts?
No way you can chug that.

06:28.783 --> 06:30.117
No, I can totally do it.

06:30.151 --> 06:32.152
I've only had, like,
four beers this morning.

06:46.434 --> 06:48.469
(cheering)

06:49.037 --> 06:50.737
(gagging)

06:50.772 --> 06:52.172
He's doing it!

06:52.207 --> 06:54.308
It's killing him,
but he's doing it.

06:54.342 --> 06:56.343
(gagging continues)

07:02.784 --> 07:05.752
So, as you can see,
sales are going very well.

07:09.724 --> 07:11.358
Griffin, you're fired!

07:11.392 --> 07:14.094
Eh, see if I care.

07:14.129 --> 07:15.596
Hello, COBRA?

07:15.630 --> 07:19.600
I'd like to pay $1,300 for
one month of health insurance.

07:25.425 --> 07:27.393
How's the job
search going, Dad?

07:27.427 --> 07:28.427
Eh, not great, Chris.

07:28.462 --> 07:29.895
I'm looking
at the paper right now.

07:29.930 --> 07:31.197
I don't see a lot here.

07:31.231 --> 07:33.566
Hey, Lois, how much
you think a Sagittarius pays?

07:33.600 --> 07:35.668
I think you're in
the wrong section, Peter.

07:35.702 --> 07:37.169
Oh, pardon me.

07:37.204 --> 07:39.305
Oh, looks like
the Dodgers just cut Pe├▒a.

07:39.339 --> 07:40.339
Might be something there.

07:40.340 --> 07:41.941
Peter, put
the paper down.

07:41.975 --> 07:43.309
Okay, kids,
off to school.

07:43.343 --> 07:44.677
Now, I know
it's picture day,

07:44.711 --> 07:46.078
but we can't
afford them anymore,

07:46.113 --> 07:47.513
so just run
behind another kid

07:47.547 --> 07:49.548
when they're getting
their picture taken.

07:53.487 --> 07:56.088
Peter, we should talk
about this job situation.

07:56.123 --> 07:57.490
Our savings are
getting pretty low.

07:57.524 --> 07:58.557
You know,
actually, Peter,

07:58.592 --> 08:00.025
there's a lot
of job training programs

08:00.060 --> 08:01.093
sponsored by the state

08:01.128 --> 08:02.995
that could help you
get the skills you need

08:03.029 --> 08:04.029
for another occupation.

08:04.064 --> 08:05.698
You know, Brian,
you could get a job.

08:05.732 --> 08:06.899
I have a job.

08:06.933 --> 08:09.068
I-I'm a writer, Peter.
I'm working right now.

08:09.102 --> 08:10.202
See this,
all of this?

08:10.237 --> 08:12.505
This is the raw material
of a picture of life

08:12.539 --> 08:14.273
that I'm gonna
paint with words.

08:14.307 --> 08:16.108
Yesterday, it took you
30 minutes

08:16.143 --> 08:17.977
to lap up a cold cut
off the floor.

08:18.011 --> 08:19.745
That's my process!

08:19.780 --> 08:20.913
It's been three weeks

08:20.947 --> 08:22.615
and you haven't had
a single job lead.

08:22.649 --> 08:23.749
Oh, that's not true.

08:23.784 --> 08:26.218
I came really close
with that job at the school.

08:26.253 --> 08:27.920
So, what makes you want
to be a crossing guard?

08:27.954 --> 08:29.622
I don't know, I just
thought it would be cool

08:29.656 --> 08:32.992
to decide which kids do
and don't get hit by a car.

08:33.026 --> 08:35.594
Well, Peter, since you've been
having such a tough time,

08:35.629 --> 08:38.597
I was thinking, maybe I
should look for a job.

08:38.632 --> 08:41.534
Lois, I'll be damned if I will
let my wife be a prostitute.

08:41.568 --> 08:44.103
What? No, I'll get
a regular job.

08:44.137 --> 08:46.071
(laughs) What,
like a lawyer?

08:46.106 --> 08:49.308
Peter, there are jobs for women
between prostitute and lawyer.

08:49.342 --> 08:50.342
Wartime nurse?

08:50.377 --> 08:51.377
We need money.

08:51.411 --> 08:52.912
I'm gonna look
for a job.

08:52.946 --> 08:55.481
(sighs) I guess you should;
and that'll give me more time

08:55.515 --> 08:57.983
to focus on expanding
my record collection.

08:58.018 --> 08:59.919
How's this one?
Oh, Bach.

08:59.953 --> 09:01.487
Is very good.
I recommend.

09:01.521 --> 09:02.688
And this one?

09:02.722 --> 09:04.123
Oh, Mozart.

09:04.157 --> 09:05.357
The boy genius.

09:05.392 --> 09:06.392
The best.

09:06.426 --> 09:07.593
Okay, how about this?

09:07.627 --> 09:09.094
Ooh, Debussy.

09:09.129 --> 09:10.463
I love Debussy.

09:10.497 --> 09:13.232
Sometimes all I can
think about is Debussy.

09:13.266 --> 09:14.967
Oh, look at the pianist.

09:15.001 --> 09:17.169
The pianist is so good
with Debussy.

09:17.204 --> 09:18.571
So, you like
his early work?

09:18.605 --> 09:20.539
Oh, yes,
when Debussy was young,

09:20.574 --> 09:22.208
that's when
you want Debussy.

09:22.242 --> 09:23.642
Okay, I'll
take these two.

09:23.677 --> 09:24.743
Very good, sir.

09:24.778 --> 09:27.179
Just make sure
you finish on the Bach.

09:27.214 --> 09:29.048
Never finish on Debussy.

09:29.082 --> 09:30.449
(applause)

09:30.484 --> 09:32.485
CROWD:
Bravo! Bravo!

09:36.857 --> 09:38.324
(deep breath)

09:38.358 --> 09:39.758
All right,
you can do this.

09:39.793 --> 09:41.026
You've shopped here for years.

09:41.061 --> 09:43.329
You know this place
like the back of your hand.

09:45.332 --> 09:48.033
Now, Mrs. Griffin, where
did you go to college?

09:48.068 --> 09:49.101
Groceries.

09:49.135 --> 09:51.103
Are you available
to work weekends?

09:51.137 --> 09:52.338
Groceries.

09:52.372 --> 09:53.372
Very impressive.

09:53.406 --> 09:54.940
This next one is
a trick question.

09:54.975 --> 09:56.141
Groceries?

09:56.176 --> 09:57.343
I'm hired.

09:57.377 --> 09:59.011
Welcome aboard.

10:03.450 --> 10:05.184
Hey, guys,
great news.

10:05.218 --> 10:07.253
You're looking at
the new assistant store manager

10:07.287 --> 10:08.320
of Stop 'N Shop.

10:08.355 --> 10:09.989
You got a job
at the grocery store?

10:10.023 --> 10:11.357
That's great!

10:11.391 --> 10:13.626
You get to see all the food
before it's famous.

10:13.660 --> 10:14.894
Well, you know
you've made it

10:14.928 --> 10:16.529
when you've got
a teenage boss.

10:16.563 --> 10:17.596
Lois, that's awesome!

10:17.631 --> 10:19.465
Now I can spend
my days at The Clam

10:19.499 --> 10:20.866
like we've always
talked about.

10:20.901 --> 10:23.202
No, Peter, if I'm gonna
be out of the house working,

10:23.236 --> 10:25.604
you're gonna have to take over
for me in the house.

10:25.639 --> 10:27.673
Wait, wait, what,
I-I got to do what you do?

10:27.707 --> 10:29.775
Spending the whole day
taking Tylenol PMs

10:29.809 --> 10:31.377
and straddling
the bath faucet?

10:31.411 --> 10:33.846
Well, the guy knows what's going
on here, I'll give him that.

10:33.880 --> 10:36.715
No, I mean, you're gonna need to
cook the meals and do laundry

10:36.750 --> 10:38.617
and take care of Stewie,
like I've been doing.

10:38.652 --> 10:39.618
Are you serious?

10:39.653 --> 10:40.753
Dad's gonna
run the house?

10:40.787 --> 10:41.954
Hey, I can do it.

10:41.988 --> 10:44.089
I mean, it can't be
any harder than that job

10:44.124 --> 10:45.958
I used to have
at the bowling alley.

10:45.992 --> 10:46.959
Bowlarama.

10:46.993 --> 10:48.460
Yes, we're open.

10:48.495 --> 10:50.863
Oh, yes, we have a wide
selection of balls

10:50.897 --> 10:53.499
that are way too heavy
or have too-small finger holes.

10:53.533 --> 10:55.701
Uh, no, you will not
be able to do anything

10:55.735 --> 10:57.970
with your wrist
for seven days afterward.

10:58.004 --> 11:00.372
Yes, sir, all of the joysticks
in the arcade

11:00.407 --> 11:03.008
are completely covered in pizza
grease, no worries there.

11:03.043 --> 11:04.276
What's that?

11:04.311 --> 11:06.912
Oh, absolutely, there is always
a group of teenagers

11:06.947 --> 11:09.381
throwing the ball real hard
and scaring everyone.

11:09.416 --> 11:12.585
No, there is no smoking,
but we do let you smoke.

11:12.619 --> 11:14.987
Yes, it's all terrible,
come on down.

11:20.327 --> 11:21.961
Why are you doing laundry
in the dishwasher?

11:21.995 --> 11:23.495
Oh, I can't use
the washing machine;

11:23.530 --> 11:25.097
it's really been
acting up lately.

11:26.499 --> 11:27.566
What the hell?

11:27.601 --> 11:29.635
What's going on
down here?

11:29.669 --> 11:31.203
This is washing
machine stuff.

11:31.237 --> 11:33.072
Go back upstairs,
suck-bag.

11:37.010 --> 11:39.178
All right, Stewie, I'm gonna
change your diaper now.

11:39.212 --> 11:41.914
Which, unfortunately, means
I have to touch your privates.

11:41.948 --> 11:44.283
All right, so here I
come with the cloth.

11:44.317 --> 11:46.352
Okay? This is
not sexual.

11:46.386 --> 11:49.488
All right, I've made contact
with your undercarriage.

11:49.522 --> 11:51.757
I am moving it upwards
with a cupped hand.

11:51.791 --> 11:53.359
I'm looking you
in the eye now.

11:53.393 --> 11:54.793
Please meet my gaze.

11:54.828 --> 11:56.028
And we're done.

11:56.062 --> 11:58.797
That was intense.

12:01.034 --> 12:02.768
All right, kids,
you are really gonna love

12:02.802 --> 12:04.536
these Cornish game hens
I cooked for dinner.

12:04.571 --> 12:06.739
Now, I don't want
to pat myself on the back,

12:06.773 --> 12:09.041
but I worked all day
getting 'em just right...

12:09.075 --> 12:10.342
Holy crap!

12:11.011 --> 12:12.044
Oh, my God.

12:12.078 --> 12:13.345
Then that means...

12:14.714 --> 12:16.181
And that also means...

12:19.352 --> 12:20.686
You know what, Peter?

12:20.720 --> 12:23.489
You tried hard, and you
still earned that wine.

12:28.762 --> 12:30.529
I'm home.

12:30.563 --> 12:32.564
Wow, Peter,
the house looks amazing.

12:32.599 --> 12:34.133
Yeah, well, let's
take off our shoes

12:34.167 --> 12:35.901
and try to keep
it that way, huh?

12:35.935 --> 12:38.170
No, really, Peter,
it seems like you've really

12:38.204 --> 12:39.805
taken to being
a househusband.

12:39.839 --> 12:41.306
Well, it hasn't
been easy.

12:41.341 --> 12:42.675
Between doing the
laundry and vacuuming,

12:42.709 --> 12:44.910
I barely had time to
put on a nice sweater

12:44.944 --> 12:47.379
and clasp a cup of
tea with two hands.

12:50.650 --> 12:52.651
(sighs):
Ah.

12:54.487 --> 12:56.922
And now to tie this sweater
around my waist

12:56.956 --> 12:59.124
and walk around
the neighborhood.

12:59.159 --> 13:01.226
Well, what do you say
I reward you

13:01.261 --> 13:02.594
for all your hard work?

13:02.629 --> 13:04.363
Geez, Lois, is that
all you think about?

13:04.397 --> 13:05.431
I'm tired.

13:05.465 --> 13:06.465
Come on, Peter.

13:06.499 --> 13:07.466
I need this release.

13:07.500 --> 13:08.934
I had a long
day at work.

13:08.968 --> 13:10.402
Oh, work.

13:10.437 --> 13:12.037
I suppose work
is why you missed

13:12.072 --> 13:13.505
Chris's father-son picnic.

13:13.540 --> 13:15.574
Peter, you're still
Chris's father.

13:15.608 --> 13:16.909
Why can't you just listen

13:16.943 --> 13:18.777
instead of trying
to fix everything?!

13:20.180 --> 13:21.313
Get in here, Peter.

13:21.347 --> 13:22.748
Don't you want to have sex?

13:22.782 --> 13:25.417
I don't think we've done it
since I started working.

13:25.452 --> 13:26.885
Yeah, I guess you're right.

13:26.920 --> 13:30.355
Come on, where's my big,
strong man?

13:30.390 --> 13:33.292
Putting on one of your
dress shirts to look sexy.

13:35.161 --> 13:36.829
(purrs)

13:36.863 --> 13:38.030
Mmm.

13:38.064 --> 13:40.132
I want to do it on top
of the comforter.

13:40.166 --> 13:41.734
I don't care if
we make streaks.

13:41.768 --> 13:42.935
<i>Well, of course you don't,</i>

13:42.969 --> 13:44.436
you're not the one
who cleans it.

13:44.471 --> 13:46.905
Peter, just shut
up and take me!

13:46.940 --> 13:48.941
(both grunting)

13:51.211 --> 13:52.678
Peter, get up! Get up!

13:52.712 --> 13:54.179
There's a caterpillar
in the bed!

13:54.214 --> 13:56.248
Oh, that's, uh...
that's me.

13:56.282 --> 13:57.282
What?

13:57.317 --> 13:58.917
How do I put this
delicately?

13:58.952 --> 14:02.254
My hog cannot partake
in the slop this evening.

14:02.288 --> 14:05.758
Peter, are you having
trouble getting... ready?

14:05.792 --> 14:07.493
Yes, obviously,
I'm having trouble!

14:07.527 --> 14:09.461
Well, somebody's gonna
have sex with me.

14:09.496 --> 14:10.529
Lois, don't say that.

14:10.563 --> 14:12.765
Quagmire will show up
like the Road Runner.

